# Everything an image doesn't need. Every file left in the context feeds the
# hash of the images that install the project (the task images, the
# dashboard), so anything listed here (docs, tests, git history, a pytest
# cache, the Flyte CLI cache, .env) would otherwise rebuild them on every
# change. A denylist, not an allowlist: Flyte matches these patterns relative
# to each folder a layer copies (`with_source_folder(src)` walks `src/`), so a
# leading `*` would drop that folder's contents.
scratch/
__pycache__/
__marimo__/
*.egg-info
.venv/
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.cache
.DS_Store
.git
.github
.codex
.opencode
.claude/skills
.claude/worktrees
.claude/settings.local.json
docs
site
tests
cli
AGENTS.md
zensical.toml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
# Local-only state: credentials and the Flyte CLI cache (which changes every
# run and would otherwise change every image hash built from this context).
.env
.flyte/
